00:51:49.570 --> 00:51:50.710
That's a joke.

00:51:50.710 --> 00:51:55.660
So the actual control that's
used on vehicles, generators,

00:51:55.660 --> 00:51:57.910
things like that, anything.

00:51:57.910 --> 00:51:59.530
It's all around you.

00:51:59.530 --> 00:52:03.910
That's all basically kind of
infinite dimensional variations

00:52:03.910 --> 00:52:05.380
on least squares.

00:52:05.380 --> 00:52:09.550
Filtering, traditional signal
processing, all least squares.

00:52:09.550 --> 00:52:11.260
Equalization, all these things.

00:52:14.892 --> 00:52:16.350
You kind of want
to make fun of it,

00:52:16.350 --> 00:52:20.900
but I wouldn't
because it's running

00:52:20.900 --> 00:52:22.880
most of the technology
we have right now.

00:52:22.880 --> 00:52:25.070
And pretty well, thank you.

00:52:25.070 --> 00:52:27.080
So could you do a little
bit better with convex?

00:52:27.080 --> 00:52:28.040
You can, yeah.

00:52:28.040 --> 00:52:34.310
But let's be humble a
